                <pb facs="1153" n="1003" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg1003"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 5359/1–4.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister King to the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Bangkok</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-03-28"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">March 28, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 312.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose a clipping from the local press
                    which appeared in all the city papers on Monday, March 25, and was given out by
                    the general adviser as a brief of the treaty and as the Government’s expression
                    on the same.</p>
                <p>There is a general feeling of satisfaction on the part of both France and Siam
                    and the opinion prevails that the treaty will be ratified in Paris without much
                    opposition.</p>
                <p>The territory exchanged differs little in extent. The districts of Battambong and
                    Siemrap, which France gets, have been considered by Mr. Strobel for a long time
                    as French in sentiment, language, location, and everything but in name.</p>
                <p>On the north the portion of Luang Prabang territory returned to Siam is a long,
                    narrow tongue of land, extending perhaps 100 miles south into the main territory
                    of Siam, following the boundary of an old former Siamese province and causing to
                    Siam a great inconvenience because of separating her territory one part from
                    another. By this new boundary this inconvenience will be removed.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hamilton King.</hi></signed></closer>






